# Draft .gitignore for the first commit. Nothing has been committed yet, so
# whatever is not excluded here enters history on the first `git add -A` and
# is painful to remove afterwards. Review before committing.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. This is the one that matters.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local state and caches -- regenerated, machine-specific, or both.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
memory.db
.serena/

# Virtual environments. `venv/` was built on macOS and does not run on
# Windows; `.venv/` is the local Windows one. Neither belongs in history —
# rebuild from requirements.txt instead.
venv/
.venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS and Office noise.
# `~$...docx` is a Word lock file, present only while the document is open.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
~$*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Corpus backups. The timestamped ones are written on every
# `verify_temporal_corpus.py triage-unlisted --apply` run and accumulate.
#
# bcs_gk_facts.json.pre-triage.bak is deliberately NOT ignored: it is the only
# copy of the corpus as it stood before the 135-fact triage, and the handover
# cites it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
bcs_gk_facts.json.*.bak

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DECIDE BEFORE COMMITTING: snapshots/
#
# 1,620 cached MediaWiki revisions, 36 MB. Arguments both ways:
#
#   Keep it   -- it is the evidence cache. Every excerpt in the ledgers was
#                drawn from these exact revisions, and re-fetching depends on
#                Wikipedia still serving those oldids. Committing makes the
#                evidence trail reproducible offline.
#   Ignore it -- 36 MB of third-party text in a research repo, fully
#                re-fetchable via `verify_temporal_corpus.py fetch` and
#                `resource_corpus.py`, and it will keep growing.
#
# Left UNIGNORED by default, because the provenance argument is the stronger
# one for this project. Uncomment the next line to exclude it.
# snapshots/
